    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1.	Quality of the report produced and submitted to the Ministry of Labour and Social Protection of Populations and recommendations in the report contribute to the state employment policies
2.1.	Number and quality of training and retraining programs for women in rural areas delivered
2.2.	Number of training and retraining programs for unemployed, unproductively self-employed, and disabled people provided
3.1.	Number of gender inclusive training and/or retraining programs for skills development in emerging industries for SMEs delivered</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1:  Report on emerging professions for Kazakhstan is prepared/Baseline 0
Output 2: Training programs for skills development are designed and delivered/Baseline 0
Output 3: Training programs for SMEs to enter emerging industries delivered/Baseline 0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 Quality of the report produced and submitted to the Ministry of Labour and Social Protection of Population and recommendations in the report contribute to the state employment policy 
2.1 Number and quality of training and retraining programs for women in the rural areas delivered
2.2 Number of training and retraining programs for unemployed, unproductively self-employed and disabled people provided
3.1 Number of gender inclusive training and/or retraining programs for skills development in emerging industries for SMEs delivered
3.2 Number of training and/or retraining services for SMEs most affected by COVID-19 provided</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 Applied Economic Research Center has conducted and completed a high quality report that identifies the most demanded professional skills in the post-covid labor market, with breakdown by levels of the National Qualifications Framework (NQF) and types of activities, and developed recommendations to the Ministry of Labour and Social Protection of Populations for preparation and delivery of the short-term online courses, on demanded professional skills, including unemployed and socially vulnerable groups of population. 
2.1 Within the framework of One Village &#x2013; One Product project more than 20 training and retraining programs for women in the rural areas have been delivered with an overall audience more than 300 people.
2.2 Within the framework of Apprenticeship scheme project, 27 training and retraining programs for unemployed, unproductively self-employed and disabled people have been provided. Out of 260 trainees, 29 are people with disabilities.
3.1 Within the framework of Women Entrepreneurship Centers, a total of 130 training and/or retraining programs for skills development in emerging industries for SMEs delivered by WECs for 2389 SMEs (IE, LLP) led by women.
3.2 Within the framework of Women Entrepreneurship Centers, a total of training and/or retraining services for SMEs most affected by COVID-19 provided by WECs for 2389 SMEs (IE, LLP) led by women.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
